From 2ffb22c770d14ea3bf0d26202564abed8ae236ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 21:22:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda/hip: the topk_moe router selection co-launched inside
 the shared-expert mmvq (+1.9% decode)

Round 31 replaced this series long-running "~1.5% per 40 launches removed"
heuristic with the right one: a merged launch pays only when the host is much
larger than the guest and memory-bound. It also ranked the remaining hide-pool
by that ratio. This is the top entry by projected gain, and the only one whose
guest is not a matvec.

The fused softmax/top-k/get_rows router selection runs as ONE workgroup, 40
times per decoded token: 2.83 us of kernel plus a ~1.3 us replay gap, almost
all of it launch latency rather than work. Its body is entirely warp-local -
no shared memory, no __syncthreads, only __shfl_xor over the 32 lanes of one
warp - so it can run as warp 0 of ONE extra block of a grouped mmvq launch
with the identical lane->expert mapping, the identical bitonic butterfly and
the identical normalisation reduction. Block-for-block bit-identical, and one
block against the host 1024 is a free ride rather than a merge.

The host is the shared-expert gate/up pair (Q8_0, 1024 blocks, 5.5 us): it
reads the same activation as the router and is independent of the entire
routed subgraph. Two halves:

- src/models/qwen35moe.cpp emits the router matvec and pins the shared-expert
  gate/up behind it, handing the logits back to build_moe_ffn through
  probs_in (which uses them as the logits verbatim). Stock order puts the pair
  AFTER the routed reduction, where ggml-alloc - which assigns buffers from
  node order - hands ffn_gate_shexp the block the expert-id list has just
  freed, and the disjointness check then correctly refuses. Reordered, the
  allocator gives gate [+0x4880,+0x5080), up [+0x5080,+0x5880), argsort
  [+0x5880,+0x5c80): tightly packed and provably disjoint. GATED ON
  n_tokens == 1 - at prefill the pair is adjacent to its GLU and llama.cpp
  fuses the three into one GEMM+GLU launch, and breaking that costs 0.9% pp512
  for nothing, since the co-launch is a decode-only path anyway.

- the grouped mmvq kernel gains one guest block at the FRONT of the grid
  (0045 measured -3.5% for the same blocks at the END; do not re-derive it),
  behind a has_topk template parameter instantiated for GGML_TYPE_Q8_0 only,
  so no other call site changes instantiation. topk_moe_cuda is refactored
  into a topk_moe_body device template that both the standalone kernel and the
  guest call, so "bit-identical" is by construction rather than by inspection.

The two merged groups are checked against EACH OTHER, not only against the
nodes between them: as separate launches the stream ordered them, inside one
kernel it does not. Every guest write (ids, weights) is checked disjoint from
every host write and host input, and the guest input (the logits) from every
host write, on actual data ranges. 0045 shipped the version without that check
and it raced only at long context.

Measured on the R9700 box (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M) against a binary built
from this patch own parent commit, control RUNPATH verified by ldd, arm order
alternated, no env set on either arm:

  candidate tg128 152.58 152.47 152.23 152.22  (mean 152.38)
  control   tg128 149.66 149.46 149.27 149.50  (mean 149.47)
  => +1.94% decode, 4/4 rounds separated. An earlier 5-round pair read +1.92%
     and the same-binary toggle reads +2.15%.

Prefill is flat by construction (decode-shape gate). Six interleaved pp512
rounds, order alternated: candidate mean 4920.3 against control 4917.0,
+0.07%.

Firing proven by kernel census diff, not a debug print: 25238 -> 23838
dispatches over 35 tokens, exactly -40.0/token, topk_moe_cuda 1400 -> 0
launches, and total kernel time 194.72 -> 192.44 ms (-65.1 us/token).

Correctness. Server greedy at the decode shape (llama-server, 6 prompts,
every completion >= 276 B, including a 1000-token prompt) is 6/6 byte
identical between co-launch on and off on the same reordered graph, against a
same-arm-twice noise control that reads 5/6 - so the co-launch is cleaner than
the harness. Perplexity on the runner corpus:

  gate shape (-c 512)         stock 3.9314  banked 3.9317  this 3.9314-3.9318
  decode path (-b 512 -ub 1)  stock 3.9409  banked 3.9338  this 3.9382

At the gate shape the graph is literally the stock build path (n_tokens != 1)
and the numbers are stock within the load-to-load spread. On the decode path
this patch moves the stack from -0.180% against stock to -0.069%: the reorder
is not byte-exact - it moves 19 of the 40 layers off llama.cpp fused
gate+up+GLU mmvq onto the grouped mmvq plus a separate unary_gated_op_quant,
two kernels computing the same SwiGLU - but it moves TOWARD stock, not away.
The co-launch half is bit-identical on its own (toggled off, the binary
reproduces the control 8.8713 exactly on gainz-corpus).

GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_TOPK_COLAUNCH=0 restores the separate topk_moe launch;
GGML_QWEN_SHEXP_GATEUP_PIN=0 restores stock node order (and with it the
byte-exact decode path, at the cost of the whole gain).
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/topk-moe-body.cuh | 417 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 417 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/topk-moe-body.cuh

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/topk-moe-body.cuh b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/topk-moe-body.cuh
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..11e9a09ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/topk-moe-body.cuh
@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@
+#pragma once
+
+#include "ggml-cuda/common.cuh"
+
+#include <cmath>
+
+// Kernel config struct - passed by value to CUDA kernel
+struct topk_moe_config {
+    bool use_sigmoid;
+    bool use_sqrt_softplus;
+    bool with_norm;
+    bool delayed_softmax;
+};
+
+// Warp-local softmax used for both the pre-top-k logits and the post-top-k delayed path.
+template <int experts_per_thread, bool use_limit>
+__device__ void softmax_warp_inplace(float (&vals)[experts_per_thread], const int limit, const int lane) {
+    float max_val = -INFINITY;
+
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+        const int  idx    = lane + i * WARP_SIZE;
+        const bool active = !use_limit || (idx < limit);
+        if (active) {
+            max_val = max(max_val, vals[i]);
+        }
+    }
+
+    max_val = warp_reduce_max(max_val);
+
+    float sum = 0.f;
+
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+        const int  idx    = lane + i * WARP_SIZE;
+        const bool active = !use_limit || (idx < limit);
+        if (active) {
+            const float val = expf(vals[i] - max_val);
+            vals[i]         = val;
+            sum += val;
+        } else {
+            vals[i] = 0.f;
+        }
+    }
+
+    sum = warp_reduce_sum(sum);
+
+    const float inv_sum = 1.0f / sum;
+
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+        const int  idx    = lane + i * WARP_SIZE;
+        const bool active = !use_limit || (idx < limit);
+        if (active) {
+            vals[i] *= inv_sum;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+template <int experts_per_thread, bool use_limit>
+__device__ void sigmoid_warp_inplace(float (&vals)[experts_per_thread], const int limit, const int lane) {
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+        const int  idx    = lane + i * WARP_SIZE;
+        const bool active = !use_limit || (idx < limit);
+        vals[i]           = active ? 1.f / (1.f + expf(-vals[i])) : -INFINITY;
+    }
+}
+
+template <int experts_per_thread, bool use_limit>
+__device__ void sqrt_softplus_warp_inplace(float (&vals)[experts_per_thread], const int limit, const int lane) {
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+        const int  idx    = lane + i * WARP_SIZE;
+        const bool active = !use_limit || (idx < limit);
+        vals[i]           = active ? sqrtf(vals[i] > 20.0f ? vals[i] : logf(1.0f + expf(vals[i]))) : -INFINITY;
+    }
+}
+
+
+// Order-preserving unsigned image of a float: for any two non-NaN floats a, b
+// (a > b) <=> (topk_moe_order(a) > topk_moe_order(b)). The selection value goes
+// in the high word and the complement of the expert index in the low word, so a
+// single unsigned 64-bit compare reproduces the stock comparison including its
+// "on a tie the lower expert index wins" rule.
+static __device__ __forceinline__ uint64_t topk_moe_key(float v, int expert) {
+    uint32_t u = __float_as_uint(v);
+    u = (u & 0x80000000u) ? ~u : (u | 0x80000000u);
+    return ((uint64_t) u << 32) | (uint64_t) (0xFFFFFFFFu - (uint32_t) expert);
+}
+
+static __device__ __forceinline__ int topk_moe_key_expert(uint64_t k) {
+    return (int) (0xFFFFFFFFu - (uint32_t) k);
+}
+
+static __device__ __forceinline__ uint64_t topk_moe_shfl_xor(uint64_t v, int mask) {
+    const int lo = __shfl_xor_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, (int) (uint32_t) (v & 0xFFFFFFFFu), mask, WARP_SIZE);
+    const int hi = __shfl_xor_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, (int) (uint32_t) (v >> 32),         mask, WARP_SIZE);
+    return ((uint64_t) (uint32_t) hi << 32) | (uint64_t) (uint32_t) lo;
+}
+
+/*
+    This kernel does the following:
+    1. optionally softmax over the logits per token [n_experts, n_tokens]
+    2. argmax reduce over the top-k (n_experts_used) logits
+    3. write weights + ids to global memory
+    4. optionally normalize the weights or apply softmax over the selected logits
+
+    It is intended as fusion of softmax->top-k->get_rows pipeline for MoE models
+*/
+// The whole computation is warp-local: no shared memory and no __syncthreads,
+// only __shfl_xor_sync over WARP_SIZE lanes. That is what lets this body run
+// unchanged as one warp of one block of a foreign kernel (0046): the lane->
+// expert mapping, the butterfly and every reduction are identical, so the ids
+// and weights are bit-identical to the standalone launch.
+template <int n_experts, bool has_bias>
+__device__ __forceinline__ void topk_moe_body(const float *         logits,
+                                              float *               weights,
+                                              int32_t *             ids,
+                                              float *               bias,
+                                              const int             n_rows,
+                                              const int             n_expert_used,
+                                              const float           clamp_val,
+                                              const float           scale_val,
+                                              const topk_moe_config config,
+                                              const int             row) {
+    if (row >= n_rows) {
+        return;
+    }
+
+    logits += n_experts * row;
+    weights += n_expert_used * row;
+    ids += n_experts * row;
+
+    constexpr int experts_per_thread = (n_experts > WARP_SIZE) ? n_experts / WARP_SIZE : 1;
+
+    float wt[experts_per_thread];
+
+    // Initialize all slots to -INFINITY
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+        wt[i] = -INFINITY;
+    }
+
+    ggml_cuda_pdl_sync();
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int i = 0; i < n_experts; i += WARP_SIZE) {
+        const int expert  = i + threadIdx.x;
+        wt[i / WARP_SIZE] = (n_experts % WARP_SIZE == 0 || expert < n_experts) ? logits[expert] : -INFINITY;
+    }
+
+    if (!config.delayed_softmax) {
+        if (config.use_sigmoid) {
+           sigmoid_warp_inplace<experts_per_thread, false>(wt, n_experts, threadIdx.x);
+        } else if (config.use_sqrt_softplus) {
+           sqrt_softplus_warp_inplace<experts_per_thread, false>(wt, n_experts, threadIdx.x);
+        } else {
+           softmax_warp_inplace<experts_per_thread, false>(wt, n_experts, threadIdx.x);
+        }
+    }
+
+    // Sanitize NaN to -FLT_MAX so the iterative argmax produces unique expert IDs.
+    // NaN comparisons always return false, which would cause the same expert to be
+    // selected repeatedly. -FLT_MAX compares normally and is still excluded by the
+    // -INFINITY sentinel used after each selection round.
+    // More relevant for the cuBLAS path. See https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/19659
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+        if (__isnanf(wt[i])) {
+            wt[i] = -FLT_MAX;
+        }
+    }
+
+    // selection_wt is only needed when bias is present (selection uses wt + bias)
+    // when no bias, we use wt directly for both selection and weight values
+    [[maybe_unused]] float selection_wt[has_bias ? experts_per_thread : 1];
+
+    if constexpr (has_bias) {
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+            selection_wt[i] = -INFINITY;
+        }
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int i = 0; i < n_experts; i += WARP_SIZE) {
+            const int expert = i + threadIdx.x;
+            selection_wt[i / WARP_SIZE] =
+                (n_experts % WARP_SIZE == 0 || expert < n_experts) ? wt[i / WARP_SIZE] + bias[expert] : -INFINITY;
+        }
+    }
+
+    //at this point, each thread holds either a portion of the softmax distribution
+    //or the raw logits. We do the argmax reduce over n_expert_used, each time marking
+    //the expert weight as -inf to exclude from the next iteration
+
+    ggml_cuda_pdl_lc();
+
+    // Sorted-list top-k.
+    //
+    // The argmax loop below runs one full 5-step __shfl_xor butterfly per
+    // selected expert, and every step waits on the previous one, so selecting
+    // top-8 on wave32 is a chain of 40 dependent cross-lane round trips with
+    // almost no work between them. This kernel is launched as a single
+    // workgroup (one row per decoded token), so that chain is the whole kernel:
+    // 39 launches per token on this model, ~3.4% of decode kernel time.
+    //
+    // Same result, fixed depth: sort the experts each lane holds into a
+    // descending list (lane-local, no cross-lane traffic), then run a 5-round
+    // xor butterfly where each round merges the two partner lists and keeps the
+    // larger half (bitonic half-cleaner + merge). The shuffles inside a round
+    // are independent, so the dependent depth is 5 rounds instead of 40, and
+    // the butterfly leaves every lane holding the same sorted top list.
+    //
+    // Selection is by the same values with the same tie-break as the loop
+    // below, the weights are the same floats, and the normalisation sum is
+    // rebuilt with the stock per-lane partials and the stock warp butterfly, so
+    // the kernel is bit-identical to the one it replaces.
+    if (!config.delayed_softmax && n_expert_used <= experts_per_thread) {
+        uint64_t key[experts_per_thread];
+        float    wv[experts_per_thread];
+
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+            const int expert = threadIdx.x + i * WARP_SIZE;
+            float     sel;
+            if constexpr (has_bias) {
+                sel = selection_wt[i];
+            } else {
+                sel = wt[i];
+            }
+            key[i] = topk_moe_key(sel, expert);
+            wv[i]  = wt[i];
+        }
+
+        // lane-local bitonic sort, descending
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int k = 2; k <= experts_per_thread; k <<= 1) {
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int j = k >> 1; j > 0; j >>= 1) {
+#pragma unroll
+                for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+                    const int l = i ^ j;
+                    if (l > i) {
+                        const bool desc = ((i & k) == 0);
+                        const bool sw   = desc ? (key[i] < key[l]) : (key[i] > key[l]);
+                        if (sw) {
+                            const uint64_t tk = key[i]; key[i] = key[l]; key[l] = tk;
+                            const float    tw = wv[i];  wv[i]  = wv[l];  wv[l]  = tw;
+                        }
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+        }
+
+        // butterfly: merge partner lists, keep the larger half, re-sort
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int mask = 1; mask < WARP_SIZE; mask <<= 1) {
+            uint64_t pk[experts_per_thread];
+            float    pw[experts_per_thread];
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+                pk[i] = topk_moe_shfl_xor(key[i], mask);
+                pw[i] = __shfl_xor_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, wv[i], mask, WARP_SIZE);
+            }
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+                const int j = experts_per_thread - 1 - i;
+                if (pk[j] > key[i]) {
+                    key[i] = pk[j];
+                    wv[i]  = pw[j];
+                }
+            }
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int j = experts_per_thread >> 1; j > 0; j >>= 1) {
+#pragma unroll
+                for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+                    const int l = i ^ j;
+                    if (l > i && key[i] < key[l]) {
+                        const uint64_t tk = key[i]; key[i] = key[l]; key[l] = tk;
+                        const float    tw = wv[i];  wv[i]  = wv[l];  wv[l]  = tw;
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+        }
+
+        float inv_sum = 1.0f;
+        if (config.with_norm) {
+            // Reproduce the stock normalisation sum exactly: each lane adds the
+            // weights of the selected experts it owns, in increasing k, and the
+            // 32 partials go through the same warp butterfly. Same addends, same
+            // per-lane order, same reduction -> bit-identical wt_sum.
+            float contrib = 0.f;
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+                if (i < n_expert_used) {
+                    const int e = topk_moe_key_expert(key[i]);
+                    if ((e & (WARP_SIZE - 1)) == (int) threadIdx.x) {
+                        contrib += wv[i];
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+            float sum = warp_reduce_sum(contrib);
+            sum       = max(sum, clamp_val);
+            inv_sum   = 1.0f / sum;
+        }
+
+        // every lane holds the same list; lane i publishes slot i
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+            if ((int) threadIdx.x == i && i < n_expert_used) {
+                ids[i]     = topk_moe_key_expert(key[i]);
+                weights[i] = (config.with_norm ? wv[i] * inv_sum : wv[i]) * scale_val;
+            }
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+
+    float wt_sum = 0.f;
+
+    float output_weights[experts_per_thread];
+
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+        output_weights[i] = 0.f;
+    }
+
+    for (int k = 0; k < n_expert_used; k++) {
+        float max_val    = wt[0];
+        int   max_expert = threadIdx.x;
+
+        if constexpr (has_bias) {
+            float max_val_s = selection_wt[0];
+
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int i = 1; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+                const int expert = threadIdx.x + i * WARP_SIZE;
+                if ((n_experts % WARP_SIZE == 0 || expert < n_experts) && selection_wt[i] > max_val_s) {
+                    max_val    = wt[i];
+                    max_val_s  = selection_wt[i];
+                    max_expert = expert;
+                }
+            }
+
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int mask = WARP_SIZE / 2; mask > 0; mask /= 2) {
+                const float val    = __shfl_xor_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, max_val, mask, WARP_SIZE);
+                const float val_s  = __shfl_xor_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, max_val_s, mask, WARP_SIZE);
+                const int   expert = __shfl_xor_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, max_expert, mask, WARP_SIZE);
+                if (val_s > max_val_s || (val_s == max_val_s && expert < max_expert)) {
+                    max_val    = val;
+                    max_val_s  = val_s;
+                    max_expert = expert;
+                }
+            }
+
+            if ((max_expert & (WARP_SIZE - 1)) == threadIdx.x) {
+                selection_wt[max_expert / WARP_SIZE] = -INFINITY;
+            }
+        } else {
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int i = 1; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+                const int expert = threadIdx.x + i * WARP_SIZE;
+                if ((n_experts % WARP_SIZE == 0 || expert < n_experts) && wt[i] > max_val) {
+                    max_val    = wt[i];
+                    max_expert = expert;
+                }
+            }
+
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int mask = WARP_SIZE / 2; mask > 0; mask /= 2) {
+                const float val    = __shfl_xor_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, max_val, mask, WARP_SIZE);
+                const int   expert = __shfl_xor_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, max_expert, mask, WARP_SIZE);
+                if (val > max_val || (val == max_val && expert < max_expert)) {
+                    max_val    = val;
+                    max_expert = expert;
+                }
+            }
+
+            if ((max_expert & (WARP_SIZE - 1)) == threadIdx.x) {
+                wt[max_expert / WARP_SIZE] = -INFINITY;
+            }
+        }
+
+        if ((k & (WARP_SIZE - 1)) == threadIdx.x) {
+            output_weights[k / WARP_SIZE] = max_val;
+        }
+
+        if ((max_expert & (WARP_SIZE - 1)) == threadIdx.x) {
+            ids[k] = max_expert;
+            if (config.with_norm) {
+                wt_sum += max_val;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    if (config.with_norm) {
+        wt_sum              = warp_reduce_sum(wt_sum);
+        wt_sum              = max(wt_sum, clamp_val);
+        const float inv_sum = 1.0f / wt_sum;
+
+        for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+            output_weights[i] *= inv_sum;
+        }
+    }
+
+    if (config.delayed_softmax) {
+        softmax_warp_inplace<experts_per_thread, true>(output_weights, n_expert_used, threadIdx.x);
+    }
+
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int i = 0; i < experts_per_thread; i++) {
+        const int idx = i * WARP_SIZE + threadIdx.x;
+        if (idx < n_expert_used) {
+            weights[idx] = output_weights[i] * scale_val;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
-- 
2.53.0

